      'WorldView 3D Site: two new switches under Look. "Google photorealistic surroundings" shows Google\'s Photorealistic 3D Tiles around the site (needs a Maps key with the Map Tiles API), also in presentations and on the client page, with Google\'s attribution. It is for looking at only: it can\'t be edited, measured, snapped to or exported. Choose "Cut out site" to keep the editable satellite ground and your buildings over the site with Google filling in around it, or "Google ground" to use Google\'s ground with its buildings pressed flat under yours; a slider raises or lowers the layer. "Style the buildings" gives the editable buildings satellite roofs and walls from the map\'s colour or material tags (or the kind of building); a building you paint keeps its own colour.',
